{"id":"R0045","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All seven eligibility criteria are met for this peer-reviewed 2026 IEEE Internet of Things Journal article on adaptive DNN partitioning and task migration across multiple UAVs.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","this article proposes a multiuncrewed aerial vehicle (UAV)-assisted mobile edge computing architecture","Primary research article proposing an adaptive DNN partitioning and migration framework.","PDF"],"E2":["T",9,"IV. SIMULATION RESULTS - Fig. 4","Performance of the proposed algorithm, where I = 10 and J = 3","Evaluated in a multi-UAV network with three to seven UAVs.","PDF"],"E3":["T",2,"I.B. Contributions and Organization","selectively executes computation-intensive DNN layers on UAVs while retaining lightweight layers on users","Distributes DNN inference layers across users and UAVs with inter-UAV task migration.","PDF"],"E4":["T",9,"IV.A. Simulation Settings","The simulation environment of this experiment is written using Python 3.7 and PyTorch","Evaluates SAC+CVX against seven baselines across convergence, energy, and UAV count.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","Date of publication 21 April 2026; date of current version 29 June 2026","Published and current in 2026 prior to the November cutoff.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","deep neural networks (DNNs) have made breakthrough progress in fields such as","Full report is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","Received 7 January 2026; revised 15 March 2026; accepted 15 April 2026","Peer-reviewed IEEE journal article with defined SAC-PER method and simulation evaluation results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0047","decision":"EXCLUDE","primary":"E3","reason":"Excluded under E3 because the evaluated workload uses synthetic generic DAG tasks rather than an actual distributed DNN inference workload, using GAT and D3QN only as an offloading optimizer.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","In this paper, we study the joint optimization of UAV deployment","Primary research article in IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing.","PDF"],"E2":["T",12,"VI.A.1. Simulation parameters setting","The system includes K = 10 GUs and M = 2 UAVs acting as","Evaluated in a multi-UAV MEC setting with two aerial edge servers.","PDF"],"E3":["F",12,"VI.A.1. Simulation parameters setting","we generate diverse task structures using a DAG generator from [36]","Evaluates synthetic DAGs rather than DNN inference; GAT and D3QN serve only as optimizers.","PDF"],"E4":["T",14,"VI.C. Optimized Deployment and Association","Fig. 8(a) compares the end time of the proposed JSPO algorithm with K-Means","Simulates JSPO and GATD3QN against K-Means, RDEG, DDQN, and D3QN baselines.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","Date of publication 3 November 2025; date of current version 6 March 2026","Published in 2025 and current in March 2026 within the window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) have emerged as effective platforms for mobile edge","Full report is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","Recommended for acceptance by F. Wang","Peer-reviewed IEEE journal article with defined JSPO/GATD3QN method and simulation results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0048","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All seven eligibility criteria are met for this peer-reviewed IEEE Transactions on Green Communications and Networking article on DAG-partitioned collaborative multi-UAV video analytics.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","This paper proposes a scalable cooperative UAV architecture for video analytics","Primary research article proposing UCAA, JDTSO, and MAPDP.","PDF"],"E2":["T",9,"VII.A.2. Simulation Setup - Table II","Number of UAVs | 5, 10, 20, 40, 60, 100, 200","Evaluated across multi-UAV swarms scaling from five to two hundred UAVs.","PDF"],"E3":["T",4,"III.A.2. Collaborative Video Analytics on UAVs","tasks are offloaded to adjacent UAVs for further classification beyond the DAG partition points","Partitions YOLOv3-tiny classifier DAGs and offloads subsequent inference across neighboring UAVs.","PDF"],"E4":["T",9,"VII. NUMERICAL RESULTS","We perform extensive simulations to evaluate our algorithm's performance under various conditions","Evaluates JDTSO and MAPDP against five baselines on latency, energy, and throughput.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","Date of publication 27 October 2025; date of current version 23 December 2025","Published in October 2025 and current in December 2025 within the window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","Collaborative multiple uncrewed aerial vehicles (UAVs) have recently demonstrated significant potential","Full report is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","The editor coordinating the review of this article was K. Wang","Peer-reviewed IEEE journal article with defined JDTSO/MAPDP methods and numerical evaluation results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0054","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All seven eligibility criteria are met for this peer-reviewed October 2026 IEEE Wireless Communications Letters study on three-tier DNN inference partitioning in STAR-RIS multi-UAV networks.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","This letter proposes semantic integrated sensing, communication, and computation in a multi-UAV network","Primary research letter proposing the GAT-HSMAO framework.","PDF"],"E2":["T",1,"II.A. Network and Heading-Coupled Star-RIS Model","K fixed-altitude UAVs serve M ground users and","Evaluated in a multi-UAV scenario with three cooperating UAVs as shown in Fig. 1.","PDF"],"E3":["T",3,"II.B. ISCC Metrics and Optimization Problem","A DNN with L layers is partitioned at (l1, l2) across UAV, MEC, and cloud","Partitions DNN inference across UAV, MEC, and cloud tiers with joint split optimization.","PDF"],"E4":["T",4,"IV. NUMERICAL RESULTS","We evaluate six schemes over five independent training seeds and 3,000 training episodes","Reports five-seed holdout, OOD, and runtime results across six comparative schemes.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","Date of publication 15 October 2026; date of current version 23 October 2026","Published in October 2026 prior to the November cutoff.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","Low-altitude aerial networks are emerging as flexible platforms for intelligent transportation","Full report is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","The associate editor coordinating the review of this article and approving it","Peer-reviewed IEEE journal letter with defined GAT-HSMAO method and five-seed evaluation results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0059","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All seven eligibility criteria are met for this peer-reviewed 2025 Chinese Journal of Aeronautics article on adaptive model switching and collaborative CNN partitioning in UAV swarms.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Article Header","FULL LENGTH ARTICLE Adaptive model switching of collaborative inference","Primary full-length research article proposing the AMSM algorithm.","PDF"],"E2":["T",10,"5.2.2. Evaluation for model partitioning algorithm","we set up 3 task UAVs and 6 relay UAVs","Evaluated with multi-UAV swarms of three or four task UAVs and six relay UAVs.","PDF"],"E3":["T",3,"3. System model","Each UAV along the communication link then sequentially infers its respective submodel","Partitions complex CNNs across task and relay UAVs for sequential collaborative inference.","PDF"],"E4":["T",8,"5.1. Simulation settings","We employ VGG16 and AlexNet as the complex model and lightweight model respectively","Simulates AMSM against seven baselines across latency, runtime, bandwidth, memory, and UAV count.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","Available online 2 May 2025","Published online in May 2025 within the 2021-2026 window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"1. Introduction","Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) have been widely used in performing tasks","Full report is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Publication Metadata Footnote","Peer review under responsibility of Editorial Committee of CJA","Peer-reviewed journal article with defined AMSM method and simulation evaluation results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0061","decision":"EXCLUDE","primary":"E3","reason":"Excluded under E3 because each UAV executes the multimodal wildfire CNN independently onboard and shares only detection alerts and navigation coordination rather than distributing inference workloads.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","This paper offers an independent drone swarm system to monitor nature and detect wildfires","Primary research article proposing a multimodal wildfire detection system.","PDF"],"E2":["T",10,"Results - Table 3","Number of UAVs | 5","Evaluated with a five-UAV swarm monitoring configuration.","PDF"],"E3":["F",7,"Algorithm 1","Apply trained model M for classification and segmentation","Each UAV runs full CNN inference locally and shares only alerts, not distributed inference.","PDF"],"E4":["T",9,"Wildfire Detection Performance","The experimental evaluation was conducted to get quantitative results, which are summarized in table 2","Reports classification, segmentation, ablation, and operational metrics on the FLAME 3 dataset.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","Published: 30 September 2025","Published in September 2025 within the 2021-2026 window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"Introduction","The use of Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) has become an efficient technological means","Full report is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",0,"Review Policy","the journal employs a strict double-blind review process","Publisher policy confirms double-blind peer review; PDF provides defined CNN method and FLAME 3 results.","https://iaiest.com/iaj/index.php/IAJSE/ReviewPolicy"]}}
{"id":"R0062","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All seven eligibility criteria are met for this peer-reviewed January 2024 IEEE Communications Magazine feature article with a four-UAV collaborative Faster R-CNN prototype evaluation.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Abstract","This article proposes a novel architecture based on an observation, orientation, decision, and action","Primary research article proposing the eCoEI architecture and prototype.","PDF"],"E2":["T",5,"EXPERIMENT SETUP","This prototype system contains four UAVs, an NVIDIA Jetson Nano developer kit","Evaluated on a four-UAV airborne computing and communication testbed.","PDF"],"E3":["T",4,"ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW","the chosen DNN inference task is partitioned over the UAVs selected in the decision period","Partitions Faster R-CNN inference across participating UAVs and re-partitions upon node loss.","PDF"],"E4":["T",6,"EFFECT OF NUMBER OF UAVS","the average frame rate of the inference result was measured","Evaluates frame rate across UAV counts and simulated node unavailability/recovery.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","IEEE Communications Magazine January 2024","Published in January 2024 within the 2021-2026 window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"INTRODUCTION","Over the last decade, due to the flexibility, maneuverability, and wide coverage","Full report is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",0,"Editorial Scope and Article Types","IEEE Communications Magazine publishes peer-reviewed feature articles alongside non-peer-reviewed columns","Peer-reviewed IEEE Communications Magazine feature article with defined OODA eCoEI method and prototype FPS results.","https://technav.ieee.org/topic/ieee-communications-magazine/"]}}
{"id":"R0063","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All seven eligibility criteria are met for this peer-reviewed May 2026 Frontiers in Neurorobotics article on cloud-to-edge speculative LLM inference and swarm coordination.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Article Header","TYPE Original Research","Original research article proposing a cognitive synergetic hierarchical framework.","PDF"],"E2":["T",11,"5.1.2. Confrontation scenarios","This 6v6 fight includes attackers, scouts, and jammers","Evaluated in multi-UAV swarm combat scenarios scaling from 2v2 to 8v8.","PDF"],"E3":["T",2,"1 Introduction","we built a cloud-to-edge acceleration protocol","Distributes DeepSeek-R1 7B draft inference on UAV edge and 70B verification on ground station.","PDF"],"E4":["T",11,"5.1.1. Simulation platform","built our environment on the JSBSim flight dynamics engine","Evaluates win rate, exchange ratio, speedup, bandwidth, and disruptions in JSBSim with Orin/RTX 3090.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","PUBLISHED 19 May 2026","Published in May 2026 prior to the November cutoff.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"1 Introduction","Modern aerial combat has pushed unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) swarms","Full report is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","REVIEWED BY Fabrice O. Morin, Technical University of Munich, Germany","Peer-reviewed original research article with defined Brain-Torso method and JSBSim evaluation results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0068","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All seven eligibility criteria are met for this peer-reviewed 2025 IEEE Access article on multi-agent meta-RL for distributed CNN layer allocation in UAV swarms.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Article Header","RESEARCH ARTICLE Multi-Agent Meta Reinforcement Learning for Reliable and Low-Latency","Primary research article proposing LDTP and MARL-meta.","PDF"],"E2":["T",12,"VI.B.5. EFFECT OF ENVIRONMENT CHANGES","The simulation began with five UAVs in the swarm","Evaluated with five to nine UAVs including dynamic joining and leaving.","PDF"],"E3":["T",7,"V.A.2. LAYERS ALLOCATIONS OPTIMIZATIONS","The CNN model is split into smaller layers and assigned to UAVs","Partitions LeNet and AlexNet layers across UAVs with intermediate feature forwarding.","PDF"],"E4":["T",10,"VI. SIMULATION RESULTS AND ANALYSIS","We used TensorFlow 1.13.1 with Python 3.7.16 to conduct the experiments","Evaluates LDTP and MARL-meta against three MARL baselines across latency, power, and memory.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","date of publication 20 May 2025; date of current version 19 June 2025","Published in May 2025 within the 2021-2026 window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","The widespread deployment of Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT) devices","Full report is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","The associate editor coordinating the review of this manuscript and approving it","Peer-reviewed IEEE Access article with defined LDTP/MARL-meta method and simulation results.","PDF"]}}
{"id":"R0071","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All seven eligibility criteria are met for this peer-reviewed 2025 IEEE ICC conference paper on LE-MHAPPO-based DNN task partitioning in heterogeneous UAV swarms.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Title and Abstract","we propose a LE-MHAPPO-based CTDE MARL scheme","Primary conference research paper proposing P-MDP and LE-MHAPPO.","PDF"],"E2":["T",5,"IV. SIMULATION RESULTS AND DISCUSSION","The simulation includes J = 2 SUAVs and I = 5 RUAVs","Evaluated in a heterogeneous swarm of two server UAVs and five receiving UAVs.","PDF"],"E3":["T",2,"II.A. Task Reception and DNN Partition Inference Model","The front part is computed locally on RUAVi, while intermediate data is compressed","Partitions ResNet-18 blocks between receiving UAVs and server UAVs for collaborative inference.","PDF"],"E4":["T",5,"IV. SIMULATION RESULTS AND DISCUSSION","we conduct simulations to evaluate the performance of the proposed LE-MHAPPO algorithm","Evaluates LE-MHAPPO against MHAPPO across reward, task delay, and energy consumption.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Conference Header","2025 IEEE International Conference on Communications (ICC): IoT and Sensor Networks Symposium","Published in 2025, wholly within the 2021-2026 window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"I. INTRODUCTION","With the rapid advancement of IoT networks, UAVs have become an integral component","Full report is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",0,"About Conference Peer Review","IEEE requires all conference papers go through the peer review process before publication","Complete IEEE ICC 2025 proceedings paper (peer-reviewed per IEEE policy) with defined LE-MHAPPO method and simulation results.","https://conferences.ieeeauthorcenter.ieee.org/understand-peer-review/"]}}
{"id":"R0073","decision":"INCLUDE","primary":"","reason":"All seven eligibility criteria are met for this peer-reviewed November 2024 Applied Sciences article on resilient distributed CNN layer allocation in UAV swarms.","e":{"E1":["T",1,"Article Header","Article End-to-End Latency Optimization for Resilient Distributed Convolutional Neural Network","Primary research article proposing the DRL-RLD system.","PDF"],"E2":["T",10,"5.2. Performance Evaluation","The performance of the proposed model is evaluated under the same conditions, including fifteen UAVs","Evaluated with five, ten, and fifteen UAVs including inoperable UAV scenarios.","PDF"],"E3":["T",3,"2. System Model","CNN layers are assigned to each UAV by the DRL model","Partitions AlexNet, VGG16, and YOLO layers across UAVs with reallocation on failure.","PDF"],"E4":["T",9,"5.1. Simulation Settings","Three CNN models were employed in the simulation: AlexNet [33], VGG16 [34], and YOLO","Simulates DRL-RLD against Heuristic, Comp-Avg, and Layer-Avg across latency, memory, and failures.","PDF"],"E5":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","Published: 22 November 2024","Published in November 2024 within the 2021-2026 window.","PDF"],"E6":["T",1,"1. Introduction","In recent decades, unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) have been employed","Full report is written in English.","PDF"],"E7":["T",1,"Publication Metadata","Received: 25 October 2024 / Revised: 16 November 2024 / Accepted: 21 November 2024","Peer-reviewed MDPI Applied Sciences article with defined DRL-RLD method and simulation results.","PDF"]}}
